# SolidJS Standards

## Folder responsibilities

```
src/pages/          Route-level screens (compose UI + local state)
src/components/ui/  Reusable primitives (Button, Input, …)
src/components/     Feature-specific or layout components
src/services/       API and domain logic (no JSX)
src/routes/         Router config only
src/lib/            Pure utilities (cn, formatters, validators)
```

## Components

- **Pages**: default export, one file per route in `src/pages/`.
- **UI & layout**: named exports; barrel re-export from `index.ts`.
- Use `splitProps` to separate local props from passthrough DOM props.
- Export a `*Props` type alongside each reusable component.
- Use `createSignal` for local page state; lift only when a second consumer appears.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — split local vs passthrough props
const [local, rest] = splitProps(props, ['label', 'class'])
return <input class={cn(baseStyles, local.class)} {...rest} />
```

## Styling

- Tailwind only. Use `cn()` from `@/lib/cn` to merge classes.
- Reuse design tokens from `src/index.css` (`bg-surface`, `text-text-muted`, `border-border`, etc.).
- Do not add CSS files per component. Do not inline hex colors — use theme tokens.

## Data & side effects

- All HTTP goes through `src/services/`. Pages call services, not `fetch`.
- Keep services as plain objects or functions — no classes.
- Type API payloads and responses explicitly.

## Icons & imports

- Icons: `lucide-solid` only.
- Path alias: `@/` for all `src/` imports. No deep relative paths like `../../`.

## What to avoid

- `createEffect` / `createMemo` unless there is a measured need.
- Global stores, context providers, or custom hooks for logic used once.
- Copy-pasting UI markup — extend or compose existing `@/components/ui` instead.
- Over-abstracted prop APIs (e.g. one mega-component with 20 optional props).
